  Yes, in casual conversation, it's not necessary to add an .i every
time a speaker switches.  It's more formal (and grammatically correct)
to do so, but in conversation amongst people (and not say, computers),
people will understand that you generally are starting new sentences,
and not continuing others.

=20

                     --gejyspa

=20

